 "relevance_note": "Case report of one child with LAD-I: 'She had been previously diagnosed with LAD-1 at 18 months of age.'; no ITGB2 variant is printed for her.",
 "method_note": "Written by a short Python script from my own reading; table-row spans were copied from the file lines by line number and checked verbatim. Case patient labelled 'patient' (rule 5). No variant rows: the paper ties no ITGB2 variant to anyone (only the general statement that LAD-1 is caused by mutations in integrin beta-2), so no 'not reported' variant row was made. Table 1 (literature review of 11 patients in 8 studies) is absent from the Markdown (heading only), so its patients get no rows. One review patient is included as 'ref 2 patient' because the Discussion gives an individual-level fact ('One patient died due to systemic fungal infection (Table 1).^2'); attributing this patient to reference 2 rests on the superscript placement and is uncertain; the paper calls the review group 'LAD', and only reference 2's title says type 1. Supplementary Table 1 is a per-day lab/medication table for the single case patient (columns are hospital days, not patients; no stacked cells). Neutrophilia and elevated IL-6 were read by comparing the values with the printed normal ranges; TNF and soluble IL-2 receptor rows were not recorded (TNF label holds an unrenderable character; sIL-2R values are within range). '-' in the Infections row is not defined, so not used. Age at last evaluation left 'not reported': she was 9 at presentation but follow-up ran at least 2 years ('stable for 2 years postoperatively') with no age given; vital status not stated. Impaired wound healing checklist left 'not reported' (wounds worsened and took 8 months to epithelialize, but the paper does not state impaired healing for her). Clinical diagnosis basis not stated (CD18 expression 5–10% is given but not as the basis). n_patients_reported and cohort_size_as_stated left null (no ITGB2-variant count; the 11 literature patients are a review set, not a cohort). No contradictions found.",
